WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:07.700
If we are given lemon juice and soap water

00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:10.219
in two different beakers, will we be able

00:00:10.220 --> 00:00:12.160
to list the difference between the two?

00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:14.860
Perhaps the list will begin with different

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:16.980
colours, appearance and so on.

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:20.420
But these are just properties that we can see.

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:22.460
Are these the only differences?

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:23.980
There are more.

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:26.740
Lemon juice tastes very sour.

00:00:27.620 --> 00:00:29.840
soap water tastes slightly bitter!

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:31.900
Please don’t try to taste it.

00:00:31.940 --> 00:00:34.600
Just trust me, it tastes slightly bitter.

00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:37.440
Is this a major difference between the two?

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:39.080
yes!

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:41.480
Taste is an important parameter, as it takes

00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:43.340
us to the chemical properties.

00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:46.100
Why does lemon juice taste sour?

00:00:46.700 --> 00:00:48.720
And why does soap water taste bitter?

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:52.720
Any idea? the answer lies in their nature.

00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:56.480
Lemon juice is an acid while soap is a base

00:00:57.360 --> 00:01:00.120
do you know what an acid is and what a base is?

00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:03.040
Lets get to know these terms first,

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:04.940
and later get into their details.

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:07.320
To begin with, we have acids.

00:01:08.420 --> 00:01:11.220
The moment we hear the term “Acid”, something

00:01:11.220 --> 00:01:13.460
scary, or something that would burn the surfaces,

00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:15.700
is what pops up in our mind.

00:01:16.280 --> 00:01:17.860
Well, that’s kind of true.

00:01:18.340 --> 00:01:20.240
Because acids are known to create a burning

00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:23.540
effect of whatever comes in contact with them.

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:26.652
They can erode the surfaces, or burn the skin

00:01:26.652 --> 00:01:28.610
when they come in contact with it.

00:01:28.610 --> 00:01:30.460
That’s how acids are!

00:01:30.940 --> 00:01:33.360
The term “Acid” comes from the Latin word

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:36.080
“Acidus ” which simply means sour!

00:01:36.090 --> 00:01:37.090
Yes!

00:01:37.090 --> 00:01:39.130
So are all acids Sour to taste?

00:01:39.130 --> 00:01:40.130
Yes they are!

00:01:40.130 --> 00:01:44.260
The intensity of sourness may vary in different acids.

00:01:44.260 --> 00:01:47.620
But the overall taste of acids is always sour.

00:01:48.500 --> 00:01:51.780
The best examples of substances that contain acids

00:01:51.780 --> 00:01:54.340
include citrus fruits like orange, lemon,

00:01:54.340 --> 00:01:56.000
lime and grapes .

00:01:56.500 --> 00:01:58.380
Now let’s talk about the soap water.

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:01.040
What nature does it have?

00:02:01.040 --> 00:02:02.920
It is basic in nature.

00:02:03.260 --> 00:02:06.780
which means soap is a base ! Or in other words, an

00:02:06.780 --> 00:02:07.500
alkali

00:02:08.220 --> 00:02:09.960
What do we mean by this?

00:02:10.580 --> 00:02:12.940
For now all we need to know is that the mild,

00:02:12.940 --> 00:02:16.040
bitter tasting compound is called a base.

00:02:16.420 --> 00:02:19.180
Bases, when added to water, give foam, and

00:02:19.180 --> 00:02:21.000
feel soapy when touched.

00:02:21.520 --> 00:02:24.460
Bases are exactly opposite to acids.

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:27.420
The best examples of bases include baking

00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:30.840
soda, washing soda, quick lime and many more.

00:02:31.580 --> 00:02:34.080
This was about acids and bases in general.

00:02:34.640 --> 00:02:37.240
Now can you tell me, what will happen if an

00:02:37.240 --> 00:02:39.660
acid and an alkali – as in a base, come

00:02:39.660 --> 00:02:40.660
together?

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:42.680
Will the solution explode?

00:02:43.460 --> 00:02:45.280
Will it give an unexpected reaction?

00:02:45.620 --> 00:02:46.880
Or something else?

00:02:47.140 --> 00:02:50.140
Well, it is something that we already know.

00:02:50.709 --> 00:02:53.760
Imagine, we mix a strong acid like Hydrochloric

00:02:53.780 --> 00:02:56.709
acid with a strong base like sodium hydroxide

00:02:57.360 --> 00:02:59.180
, what will be the result then?

00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:02.855
the reaction yields sodium chloride and water

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:05.520
Sodium chloride is the common salt used

00:03:05.530 --> 00:03:06.590
by us.

00:03:06.590 --> 00:03:09.500
So, an acid with a base gives us salt and

00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:12.780
water . this is a generalised reaction.

00:03:13.640 --> 00:03:16.480
Salts are the products of reaction between

00:03:16.480 --> 00:03:17.800
an acid and a base.

00:03:18.150 --> 00:03:20.920
But now tell me one thing, how do we understand

00:03:20.920 --> 00:03:23.420
whether a compound is acidic or basic?

00:03:24.060 --> 00:03:25.620
Can we taste it every time?

00:03:26.460 --> 00:03:28.780
If we are given a solution of concentrated

00:03:28.780 --> 00:03:31.120
sulphuric acid, how are we supposed to know

00:03:31.120 --> 00:03:32.620
it's nature?

00:03:32.620 --> 00:03:33.980
Its not possible to bear even a drop of

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:35.120
it on your skin.

00:03:36.180 --> 00:03:39.100
So tasting the solution is just out of thequestion.

00:03:39.840 --> 00:03:42.600
So,now how do we say that this is an acidic solution?

00:03:43.080 --> 00:03:46.180
There has to be a way to figure it out.

00:03:46.520 --> 00:03:49.280
The solution has to undergo a few tests.

00:03:49.940 --> 00:03:52.040
The substance used to check whether the compound

00:03:52.040 --> 00:03:54.820
is acidic or basic is called an indicator

00:03:55.960 --> 00:03:59.200
The indicators indicate by changing their colours!

00:03:59.900 --> 00:04:02.280
Indicators when added with acids or bases,

00:04:02.280 --> 00:04:04.280
show a change in colour.

00:04:05.100 --> 00:04:07.840
That is how it becomes convenient for us to

00:04:07.848 --> 00:04:10.200
find out whether the compound is acidic or

00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:11.520
basic.

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:14.320
But what kind of substances are used as indicators?

00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:19.700
Next, we will look at the various indicators .

